        "text": "1.) I was able to run `02_postgres_taxi_scheduled.yaml` and `02_postgres_taxi.yaml` with my configuration\/the config you gave in the video. The given config in the github repo didn’t work on macOS. ~Just said failed, when running the flows. I couldn’t really inspect\/find a more descriptive error message. Maybe problem with database~\n\nUPDATE: had to fix `02_postgres_taxi.yaml`\n```pluginDefaults:\n  - type: io.kestra.plugin.jdbc.postgresql\n    values:\n      url: jdbc:<postgresql:\/\/postgres:5432\/nyc_taxi>\n      username: postgres\n      password: postgres```\nBut this is still lacking Athena, right?\n\nShould I follow <https:\/\/kestra.io\/blueprints\/ingest-to-datalake-event-driven|this “guide”> to setup Athena? How do I setup Athena on AWS (haven’t tried, just asking for pitfalls and best settings)? How can I modify `06_gcp_taxi_scheduled.yaml` and `06_gcp_taxi.yaml`  to run on  aws?\n\nWhat do I have too configure to connect to the RDS database from my local computer (macOS 15.3) with DBeaver? Always getting a timeout error. I can connect with `pgcli` on my EC2 instance. Do I have to ssh-tunnel with DBeaver to the instance first? UPDATE: It worked with a ssh tunnel (followed <https:\/\/medium.com\/@dogukannulu\/dbeaver-and-amazon-rds-mysql-connection-b4b4a345d885|this guide)>.\n\n(I also watch <https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=3q8FbiR-t8g|this> to familiarize with Kestra)\n\nThe main channel is so cluttered, it would take hours to search for help,",
